option.value:
@startuml ' Escala — high-level system architecture. ' One Angular client, two Java (Spring Boot) services, one PostgreSQL database per service. ' The services talk asynchronously through RabbitMQ; no service reads another service's database.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle skinparam packageStyle rectangle skinparam linetype polyline skinparam nodesep 90 skinparam ranksep 120 skinparam defaultTextAlignment center skinparam ArrowFontSize 11 skinparam padding 4
left to right direction
title Escala — High-level system architecture
legend top right |= Colour |= Element | |<#E8F5E9> | Client (Angular) | |<#E3F2FD> | escala-api (Java) | |<#FFF3E0> | elegibilidade-worker (Java) | |<#EEEEEE> | Messaging / external | Solid line: synchronous. Dashed line: asynchronous. endlegend
actor "Firefighter" as FF actor "Duty chief" as DC actor "Commander" as CMD
package "Client" #E8F5E9 { component "web\nAngular PWA" as WEB }
package "escala-api" #E3F2FD { component "escala-api\nSpring Boot\nREST API" as API database "escala-db\nPostgreSQL" as ADB }
package "Messaging" #EEEEEE { queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ }
package "elegibilidade-worker" #FFF3E0 { component "elegibilidade-worker\nSpring Boot" as WK database "elegibilidade-db\nPostgreSQL" as WDB }
package "External systems" #EEEEEE { component "IPMA\nfire risk data" as IPMA component "Language model" as LLM }
' Users FF --> WEB DC --> WEB CMD --> WEB
' Client -> escala-api WEB --> API : REST/JSON\n(HTTPS)
' Each service owns its database API --> ADB : SQL WK --> WDB : SQL
' Asynchronous messaging: one line per service, both directions API <..> MQ : requests out\nresults in MQ <..> WK : requests in\nresults out
' External systems WK --> IPMA : HTTPS WK --> LLM : HTTPS
@enduml

